WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.208
S(n) numbers a derivational stage.

2
00:00:04.208 --> 00:00:09.035
It does not number a simplex dimension.

3
00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:13.738
At stage zero, <> is one opaque whole.

4
00:00:13.738 --> 00:00:21.163
Supplying that inscription leaves the
admitted regime empty.

5
00:00:21.163 --> 00:00:25.000
A supplied mark admits nothing.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.367
At stage one, <a> is one opaque token.

7
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:34.746
Supply of that mark is a no-op.

8
00:00:34.746 --> 00:00:39.831
Admission is a later explicit event.

9
00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:50.000
The stage index is not a point, and it is
not a one-dimensional simplex.

10
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.469
At stage two, reading L retains the opaque
wholes <a> and <ab>.

11
00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:00.069
The inscription <ab> is not a pair inside
the regime.

12
00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:05.191
Glyph identity, component count, and order
are unavailable.

13
00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:09.965
A later grammar may parse the same bytes
as two glyphs.

14
00:01:09.965 --> 00:01:15.000
That parser is a new interpretation, not
the source token.

15
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.407
Stage three asks those two opaque data to
be separable under a stated item cost.

16
00:01:22.407 --> 00:01:26.389
That cost does not force a triangular
face.

17
00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:28.796
A stage is not a triangle.

18
00:01:28.796 --> 00:01:36.732
A simplicial complex can be supplied later
as a realization, and a realization has no

19
00:01:36.732 --> 00:01:40.000
authority to create the next stage.
